00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:03.470 align:start position:0%
firefighters spent another night  battling some of the deadliest wildfires  in California history  those fires have killed at least 17  people in Northern California more than  2000 structures are destroyed there are  at least 17 dangerous fires burning  right now in the state much of the  destruction is in the heart of  California's wine country north of San  Francisco and we're hearing new stories  this morning about the terrifying rush  to escape those flames Carter Evans is  in Santa Rosa where the fires burned a  huge area Carter good morning good  morning home after home after home just  burned beyond recognition this was  someone's living room here the fence to  their side yard entire neighborhoods  like this one were just incinerated now  crews are combing through the wreckage  as as many as 190 people have been  reported missing  but the sheriff says that may be due to  all the chaos of the evacuations the  flames were moving so fast through  neighborhoods Tuesday night firefighters  couldn't reach homes in time to save  them stunned residents watched  helplessly as these new fires burned  south east of Santa Rosa  before-and-after photos there show  suburbs turned into wastelands as his  fire progressed  Deputy Fire Chief Scott McLean says his  teams were overwhelmed how do you even  fight a fire like this you really can't  in this case honestly you can't and  we're still in it I still have a ways to  go the fire forced frantic evacuations  Sunday night as emergency calls went out  across the region almost 80 cellphone  towers were damaged or lost power making  it difficult for families to reconnect  with their missing loved ones the fire  tore through 20,000 acres in 12 hours on  Monday that's the equivalent of burning  more than an entire football field every  three seconds that distance in just a  matter of hours  is phenomenal this newly released video  shot by a sheriff's deputy when flames  first broke out Sunday night shows the  intensity of the fire from the start  once the flames swept through nothing  but charred remains were left one  winemaker in Napa County says at least  five of the region's wineries have been  destroyed or seriously damaged and  grapes are being affected by the smoke  even at wineries untouched by flames now  this is what this neighborhood looked  like before and here is what it looks  like now you can see burnt out hulks of  cars just about everywhere you look and  firefighters tell me this is significant  they say it's an indication of how fast  this fire was truly moving people did  not even have time to get in their cars  and go to safety some were running for  their lives as for the winds today  Charlie they're supposed to pick back up  again and that could bring this fire  roaring back to life Carter thanks
 

